this Nigerian man has just one goal to  go to Europe and leave a life of poverty  behind Albert is an unemployed business  manager and determined to reach Europe  at any cost his passage is already  organized people traffickers will take  him across the Sahara Desert to Libya  and then by sea to Italy I've tried so  many times many times past my CV some  oil many places still no job  many Nigerians are trying to flee the  Islamist extremist militia Boko Haram  the group has been terrorizing the north  of the country for years others like  Albert come from the slums of Nigeria's  big cities they simply want to escape  poverty corruption and social injustice  this year alone more than 12,000  Nigerians tried to reach Italy by boat  it's not known how many didn't make it  the authorities in Nigeria seem  reluctant to discuss the issue all our  requests for interviews were denied  every month thousands of Nigerian seek  their home country and risked their  lives trying to reach Europe meanwhile  Nigeria's leaders remain silent  something they often accused of doing  when it comes to sensitive political  issues but even I Jarius media are  practically ignoring the topic  television journalist if young a cop is  one of the few Nigerian journalists who  regularly report about immigration he  tells us that many of his colleagues  regard the problem as a European one a  cop thinks it's more important to find  the root cause of why so many Africans  want to leave her homeland it isn't that  the African journalist or the media here  are not aware of the impacts that  migration has caused better really  African media we don't seem to give too  much importance or attention to the  migration issue which I think it's wrong  more reports about migration would do  nothing to deter Albert from making his  plan a reality tonight he's hunkered  down in an old guest house tomorrow the  journey continues watching football  makes the dream of living in Europe feel  closer than ever before
 

